local - local-0003-TI-drm-bridge-cdns-dsi-Remove-duplicate-code-for-phy.patch TI fix 28fe7134779c (TI: drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: Remove duplicate code for phy cleanup) from ti-linux-6.12.y, newer than the TI base. The base calls phy_power_off() and phy_exit() twice in cdns_dsi_bridge_atomic_post_disable() (TI FROMLIST 441a249deef6 plus stable 750442b99e0a), so the phy-core counts go to -1 and the D-PHY power_on op is skipped after the first disable. Since cip11 0672 programs the PLL in power_on, the D-PHY PLL then stays at the first mode's rate on a mode change (seen on the ECU-1270 board 2026-11-16); TI also reports DSI lanes not ready after system resume. Same patch-id as TI's commit; ti-linux-6.18.y has a single block too.
